From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: do not check the Beacon of another BSS with
 an AP's BIGTK

An AP vif holds the BIGTK of its own links alone. For a Beacon with a
MME, ieee80211_rx_h_decrypt() takes the BIGTK of the key index from the
station or from the link, and an OBSS has no station, so the AP's own
BIGTK checked the OBSS Beacon. The MIC failed (RX_DROP_U_MIC_FAIL)
before ieee80211_rx_h_mgmt_check(), so no OBSS Beacon with beacon
protection reached cfg80211_report_obss_beacon_khz() and hostapd never
learned such a neighbour, for example its BSS Color.

Let a Beacon whose transmitter is none of the AP's own addresses go on
without a key, so that ieee80211_rx_h_mgmt_check() reports it. Beacons
of the AP's own links, and every Beacon on a non-AP interface, take the
BIGTK as before. ieee80211_drop_unencrypted_mgmt() is unchanged.

ieee80211_rx_h_mgmt_check() also runs the software BSS Color collision
check, ieee80211_rx_check_bss_color_collision(), on the Beacons it now
receives. A neighbour with beacon protection and the AP's own colour
now raises a colour collision, as an unprotected one does.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>

--- a/net/mac80211/rx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/rx.c
@@ -2107,6 +2107,15 @@ ieee80211_rx_h_decrypt(struct ieee80211_
 		    (status->flag & RX_FLAG_IV_STRIPPED))
 			return RX_CONTINUE;
 
+		/*
+		 * An AP holds the BIGTK of its own links alone. The Beacon of
+		 * another BSS goes on unverified to ieee80211_rx_h_mgmt_check(),
+		 * which reports it as an OBSS Beacon.
+		 */
+		if (rx->sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP &&
+		    !ieee80211_is_our_addr(rx->sdata, hdr->addr2, NULL))
+			return RX_CONTINUE;
+
 		if (mmie_keyidx < NUM_DEFAULT_KEYS + NUM_DEFAULT_MGMT_KEYS ||
 		    mmie_keyidx >= NUM_DEFAULT_KEYS + NUM_DEFAULT_MGMT_KEYS +
 				   NUM_DEFAULT_BEACON_KEYS) {
